# Completion review — add-model-benchmark-search

**Status:** local source fix and focused verification complete; PR, deployment,
and controlled live acceptance are pending.

## Root cause

The scheduled queue called the low-level search handler as
`duckduckgo-free` with empty credentials. On the live service, the latest 100
stored runs contained 45 `duckduckgoFree:error` receipts. The direct
DuckDuckGo endpoint had also timed out from the host. The running OmniRoute
container is still on the pre-fix image.

## Fix

- Route scheduled discovery through the shared credential-resolving search
  executor and explicitly select `ollama-search`, which resolves its key from
  the active `ollama-cloud` connection.
- Stop before the request unless its registry cost is zero. Reject any result
  whose provider ID changes or whose reported search cost is nonzero.
- Leave search alternates unset. Search results remain review-required, and
  strict-SO extraction remains pinned to the existing exact free connection.

## Verification

- RED reproduced the missing `validateOllamaSearchResponse` guard. Queue-level
  failure coverage verifies an Ollama HTTP error records `source_error`, saves
  no evidence, and sends no strict-SO request. The focused suite passes 30/30.
- `npm run check:docs-all` exits 0; it reports 98 existing potential-drift
  warnings. Prettier and `git diff --check` pass for all changed files.
- `npm run typecheck:core` exits 2 with 757 TypeScript errors in unrelated
  project files. It reports no diagnostics for either changed TypeScript file.
- Code Simplifier applied to the owned source and test changes.
- Independent Luna-xhigh review confirmed the credential mapping, exact
  zero-cost provider pin, no-alternate behavior, and unchanged strict-SO path.
  Follow-up review confirmed the queue-coverage test rejects any unrecognized
  fetch URL and found no remaining findings.

## Live state and remaining work

- At 2026-10-26 16:22 UTC, the healthy production container still used image
  `sha256:f4decfc1a233e00b5b404f3dfa25bf020aebc12a4d79b1510d736a038ca0ab5f`.
- Read-only checks found `AA_API_KEY` set in the running container, three
  active `ollama-cloud` API-key connections, and 3,999 queue rows: 3,770
  retain the prior missing-AA-key error, 37 are review-required, 9 scored, and
  50 have no evidence. Models.dev sync is enabled. A successful startup sync
  launches the queue drain, which chains through eligible batches of 100.
- The catalog lists 1,000 Ollama Search requests/month, but its exact live
  remaining allowance has not been established. No paid search fallback is
  configured by this fix; the queue's monthly-quota guard remains open work.
- Still required: pre-inference live checks, PR merge and main-image deploy,
  exact deployed source/image receipt, one controlled post-deploy search and
  strict-SO acceptance, and a verified quota-usage receipt before judging the
  full-catalog run complete.
